# Build outputs
/target/
# Any crate's, not only the workspace root's. `cargo xtask mutants` writes its
# scratch diff under `target/`, and cargo-mutants builds each mutant in a copy
# of the tree -- which is how `xtask/target/xtask-mutants/in-diff.patch` was
# committed. A leading slash anchors to this directory and nowhere else.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this workspace produces a binary, so reproducible
# builds and supply-chain auditing depend on it. Do not add it here.

# archwarden's own cache directory (when dogfooding).
# Only the cache — .archwarden/ also holds artefacts users are meant to commit:
# AGENT_RULES.md, and baseline.json, which is a record of accepted debt and is
# worthless if it does not travel with the repository.
.archwarden/cache/

# Personal tooling, not required to work on this project
.ai-jail

# Claude Code's per-machine settings. `.claude/settings.json` IS committed --
# it carries the session hook that sweeps what a previous session left, and a
# hook that only exists on one machine is a hook nobody else benefits from.
# This one is the personal half: permission allowlists that name one person's
# habits.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python bytecode from the scripts' own tests.
__pycache__/

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Env files
.env
.env.local

# Test artefacts
tmp/
*.snap.new

# The platform packages are generated from release artifacts at publish time.
npm/dist/
npm/**/node_modules/

# cargo-mutants scratch output
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Python bytecode from the release scripts. Version-specific, regenerated on
# every run, and committed by accident in M9.
__pycache__/
